<% content_for :title, "Privacy Policy - Pairin" %>
<% content_for :description, "How Pairin collects, uses, and protects your data." %>

<div class="px-6 md:px-16 lg:px-24 py-16 md:py-20 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
  <a href="<%= root_path %>" class="text-sm font-bold text-purple hover:underline">&larr; Back to Pairin</a>

  <h1 class="font-display font-extrabold text-4xl md:text-5xl tracking-tight leading-none mt-6 mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm mb-10">Last updated <%= Date.current.strftime("%B %-d, %Y") %></p>

  <div class="prose max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-6">
    <p>
      Pairin ("we", "us", "our") runs <a href="<%= root_url %>" class="text-purple font-bold">pairin.dev</a>, a
      community for finding pair-programming partners. This page explains what we collect, why, and how you can
      control it. Pairin is currently in beta, and this policy will be updated as the product matures.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-black mt-10 mb-3">What we collect</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
      <li><strong>Account information</strong> &mdash; your email address and password (stored encrypted) when you sign up, plus any profile details you choose to add (name, bio, tech stack, avatar).</li>
      <li><strong>Activity data</strong> &mdash; pair requests, offers, sessions, and retro feedback you create or submit while using Pairin, so the product can function.</li>
      <li><strong>Usage analytics</strong> &mdash; we use <a href="https://posthog.com" class="text-purple font-bold" rel="noopener">PostHog</a> to understand how Pairin is used (pages visited, features used) so we can improve it. This may include session replay of in-app usage. We do not sell this data.</li>
      <li><strong>Essential cookies</strong> &mdash; a session cookie and a CSRF token cookie, required to keep you signed in and to protect your account from cross-site request forgery. These aren't used for advertising.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-black mt-10 mb-3">How we use it</h2>
    <p>
      To run the core product (matching you with pairing partners, showing your requests and sessions), to send
      transactional email (confirmations, pairing notifications, retro nudges) via our email provider, Mailjet, and
      to understand and improve how Pairin is used. We don't use your data for ads, and we don't sell it to third
      parties.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-black mt-10 mb-3">Retro visibility</h2>
    <p>
      Session retros are private between the two participants by default. You choose, per retro, whether to make it
      public to other signed-in Pairin members via Session Summaries. Nothing you write is shared publicly unless
      you explicitly opt in.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-black mt-10 mb-3">Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      You can update or delete your profile information at any time from your account settings. To request full
      deletion of your account and associated data, contact us using the details below.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-black mt-10 mb-3">Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy or your data? Reach us at
      <a href="mailto:hello@pairin.dev" class="text-purple font-bold">hello@pairin.dev</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
